## Charismatic – A player who naturally lifts teammates’ spirits and energizes the group.
## Example: Ronaldinho — joyful, expressive, always smiling on and off the pitch.

## Introverted – Quiet and self-contained, focusing inward rather than leading vocally.
## Example: Lionel Messi — leads by example rather than words.

## Aggressive – Intense, fiery, sometimes emotional or confrontational.
## Example: Serena Williams — channels emotion and intensity into her play.

## Laid-back – Calm, humorous, often relaxed even under pressure.
## Example: Klay Thompson — rarely shows stress, even in big NBA moments.

## Disciplined – Consistent, methodical, and organized in daily habits.
## Example: Cristiano Ronaldo — known for strict diet, recovery, and training routines.
